    "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\n`mask_history=True` should train only on the final assistant turn. With an\n`efficient_eos` template, the SFT processor masks historical response tokens\nbut still inserts supervised EOS labels into historical source spans.\n\nFor a three-turn conversation using `bailing` or `hy_dense_7b`, one historical\nEOS remains in the labels consumed by shifted causal-LM loss. The final\nresponse is therefore not the only training target. This affects ordinary\nand packed SFT preprocessing.\n\nSkip the historical EOS insertion when `mask_history` is enabled. The final\nEOS remains supervised. Training on every turn and templates without\n`efficient_eos` keep their existing behavior.\n\nAdd offline regression cases using the real registered templates and a local\nbyte-level tokenizer. The expected targets come from encoding individual\nassistant responses, and the assertion checks labels after the causal shift\nso an ignored label at position zero cannot produce a false positive.\n\n## Validation\n\n```bash\nCUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 PYTHONPATH=src HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 \\\n  python -m pytest tests/data/processor/test_supervised.py -q -k eos_history_labels\n```\n\n- Original implementation: 4 failed, 20 passed. The failures cover three-turn\n  history masking with `bailing` and `hy_dense_7b`, with and without packing.\n- Fixed implementation: 24 passed. Controls cover single-turn input,\n  training on all turns, and the non-efficient-EOS `llama2` template.\n- Full `tests/data/processor/test_supervised.py` with Hub access enabled:\n  28 passed, including the four existing dataset/tokenizer tests.\n- Changed-file pre-commit, Ruff checks/format, the processor directory license\n  check, and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nValidation ran on CPU with Python 3.12. No end-to-end fine-tuning run or model\nquality benchmark was performed; this change corrects the label mask.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the contributor guideline?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?\n",
